Third-party components
----------------------

The programs built from this repository are cmd/ims, cmd/ue and cmd/oss.
cmd/ims and cmd/ue link these Go modules, and cmd/oss links no
third-party module. Each module keeps its own licence, which Go keeps
with the module source:

  github.com/fiorix/go-diameter/v4   BSD 3-Clause
  github.com/ishidawataru/sctp       Apache License 2.0
  github.com/miekg/dns               BSD 3-Clause
  go.yaml.in/yaml/v3                 MIT and Apache License 2.0
  golang.org/x/net, golang.org/x/sys BSD 3-Clause

The NOTICE files of two of these modules say:

  go.yaml.in/yaml/v3: Copyright 2011-2016 Canonical Ltd. Licensed under
  the Apache License, Version 2.0.

  github.com/ishidawataru/sctp: This source code includes following
  third party code - ipsock_linux.go : licensed by the Go authors, see
  GO_LICENSE file for the license which applies to the code.

The tests also use github.com/emiago/sipgo (BSD 2-Clause) and the modules
it depends on (MIT and BSD 3-Clause), and
github.com/santhosh-tekuri/jsonschema/v6 (Apache License 2.0) with the
module it depends on, golang.org/x/text (BSD 3-Clause).

The container images install third-party programs from public images and
package repositories, among them pjsua (PJSIP) and tshark (Wireshark),
which are licensed under the GNU GPL. They run as separate programs; the
images do not link them with the code of this repository.

Data files
----------

  deploy/announcements/*.wav  Synthesised by a program in this repository.
  **/*.amr                    A sine tone encoded with opencore-amr and
                              vo-amrwbenc (tools/amrgen).
  Milenage test values        The test sets of 3GPP TS 35.208.

  slides/internal/pptx/testdata/ecma376/*.xsd
                              Unchanged copies of XML schemas that Ecma
                              International publishes with ECMA-376, used
                              by the tests to validate the pptx the slide
                              generator writes. Copyright (c) Ecma
                              International. The README beside them names
                              the editions and carries the copyright
                              notice and licence of Ecma International,
                              which allow the files to be copied and
                              distributed unchanged. The licences of this
                              repository do not apply to them.
